        <type><ref refid="msvc__stdint_8h_1aec6fcb673ff035718c238c8c9d544c47" kindref="member">uint64_t</ref></type>
        <definition>uint64_t LinearCongruentialGenerator::next</definition>
        <argsstring>(size_t nbits=64, size_t niter=1)</argsstring>
        <name>next</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="clang-builtin-opencl_8h_1a028b7cbca0d37bbc9bc219370525227f" kindref="member">size_t</ref></type>
          <declname>nbits</declname>
          <defval>64</defval>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="clang-builtin-opencl_8h_1a028b7cbca0d37bbc9bc219370525227f" kindref="member">size_t</ref></type>
          <declname>niter</declname>
          <defval>1</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Return the next value in the sequence. If nbits is specified, then only the low-order bits are randomized and the high order bits are always cleared. For instance, to get only positive values for casting to a 32-bit signed integer, use nbits=31. The <computeroutput>niter</computeroutput> indicates the number of values that should be consumed, all of which are exclusive-ORed together to create the return value. If <computeroutput>niter</computeroutput> is zero this function returns zero without consume any values. </para>        </detaileddescription>
